    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "A system failure triggering crisis struck when Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2 tripped offline, a shutdown event that initiated disorder across the grid. In response, the grid authority declared an emergency, activating an alert declaration to contain the threat. To enforce grid discipline and prevent a massive capacity loss, authorities issued a load management order, stabilizing the power grid.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Chronic operational decay and demand pressure straining system limits created a high demand period that left the grid vulnerable. The failure of the offline generator triggered a grid incident, prompting the crisis manager to issue an emergency declaration. This decisive action, enforcing grid discipline through emergency measures, averted a generation shortfall in the region's energy sector.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "why-2",
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.8
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The failure that initiated disorder involved a power plant component, a generating unit that experienced an equipment failure. This triggered a grid management action: the authority declaring emergency in the Visayas region. By ordering load shedding, a control action for grid stabilization, the decision-makers contained the power shortage to under a thousand megawatts, restoring order to the energy infrastructure.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
